  "title": "Anglo-Zanzibar War: How Did a War Last Only 38 Minutes?",
  "description": "The Anglo-Zanzibar War of 1896 is the shortest war in history: it lasted less than an hour. So how did a war end before breakfast?\n\nIn August 1896 the sultan of Zanzibar died, and his cousin Khalid bin Barghash seized the palace without British approval. Britain set a deadline of nine in the morning. At 9:02 the Royal Navy opened fire, his royal yacht HHS Glasgow sank in minutes, and by about 9:40 the flag was down. Around 500 people were killed or wounded, while one British sailor was hurt. Khalid fled to the German consulate, and his supporters were made to pay for the shells.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a strange true story every day. What is the shortest thing you have ever waited in line for? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #anglozanzibarwar #shortestwar #history #stickstory",
